window.docContents[229].resolve({"/Blog-posts/Prescriptive-versus-descriptive/#The-Den--Blog-posts--Prescriptive-versus-descriptive":{"contents":"Motivation\n\nMany discussions and debates I have with my friends go in circles and get messily tangled because of implicit mixing-up between descriptive and prescriptive statements; people (including me) tend to use both modes, and switch back and forth between them without making it clear.\n\nFirst, I'll give a brief overview of what I take each word to mean; feel free to skip if you're bored.\n\nClassic examples of descriptivism versus prescriptivism\n\nThe field of linguistics in particular, which I hold fondly in my heart, is greatly concerned about\n\nHow they might fit together\n\n","context":"The Den\u0009Blog posts","header":"3.2. Prescriptive versus descriptive","id":"/Blog-posts/Prescriptive-versus-descriptive/#The-Den--Blog-posts--Prescriptive-versus-descriptive"}});